<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
	Which block attributes WPML translates when a page is translated.

	WPML reads this file by itself, from the plugin root; without WPML it does
	nothing. That is why there is ONE for all modules (1.1.0; until then it
	belonged to the forms plugin): a module with attributes to translate adds
	its <gutenberg-block> entries here, in the same commit as the module. It is
	one of the three shared files (see includes/class-modules.php).

	What a <key> does (WPML 5, measured 17-10-2026 on Lavandería local): when
	a page is sent to translation, WPML reads these attributes from the block
	comment of every block of that type and offers each value as a field of
	the translation job (Advanced or Classic Translation Editor); when the job
	is completed, it rebuilds the translated page FROM THE ORIGINAL, replacing
	only these values. So an attribute that is NOT declared is copied as it
	is from the original, on every translation update: a manual change on the
	translated page lasts until the next update. «label» is the field title
	the translator sees; type="link" makes it a link field (a URL that may
	change per language). Without WPML, or for a block not listed, nothing.

	The criterion: an attribute goes in if a PERSON reads it, on the page or
	in an email (a label, a placeholder, a message, an aria-label, an alt
	text), or if it is a URL that may change per language (the privacy page,
	a map in another language). It stays out if it is a key, a number, an
	enum, an id or a technical value: translating it would break something or
	mean nothing. Declaring it does not force anyone to translate it: left
	untranslated, the translated page shows the original.

	How to maintain:
	- A new string attribute in a block.json goes in here OR into EXCLUDED of
	  tests/wpml-blocks.test.mjs, with its reason, in the same commit; that
	  level 1 test fails otherwise (and if something here no longer exists in
	  the block.json). Number, boolean and enum attributes are left out by
	  the test on their own.
	- Edge cases, by name:
	  · The recipient of a notification («to», «replyTo») is NOT translated,
	    so the translator cannot redirect the emails. If a site needs a
	    different recipient per language, it is set by hand on the translated
	    page (and redone after each translation update, see above).
	  · «name» and «formId» are not translated either: they are keys, and
	    translating them would split the submissions log and the markers.
	  · The dropdown's «defaultOption» is not either: it is the POSITION of
	    the option, and since «options» is translated line by line without
	    changing the order, the translated page preselects the same option on
	    its own (see modules/forms/includes/class-preselect.php). A translator
	    who reorders the options shifts it.
	  · The phone of the WhatsApp button and of the map: the same number in
	    every language.
	  · The form's «title» IS translated although the page does not show it:
	    it is the default subject of the emails («Site: title») that the
	    sender of the acknowledgement reads.
	- The traps:
	  · The texts used by default when the attribute is empty (the «Send»
	    button, the consent, the WhatsApp label) do NOT go through here, they
	    come from the .po. If they are filled in on the original site, then
	    they do have to be translated here.
	  · An attribute bound with Block Bindings (the map bound to a location,
	    the WhatsApp message bound to the company details) shows the bound
	    value whatever its saved value is: it is translated where the source
	    lives (the location post, String Translation), not here.
	  · The aliases with the names from before 1.0.0 (armazon-forms/…,
	    armazon-site/consent, armazon/…) are NOT declared: the migrator
	    rewrote that content (Lavandería, the only site that had it); an old
	    block left over shows its original text in every language.
	  · Every attribute of a <key> must be one WPML's XSD admits (label, type,
	    sub-type, encoding, search-method…): one invalid attribute drops the
	    WHOLE file (see the custom-types comment below).
-->
<wpml-config>
	<gutenberg-blocks>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/form" translate="1" label="Form">
			<key name="title" label="Form title (default email subject)" />
			<key name="successMessage" label="Success message" />
			<key name="errorMessage" label="Error message" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/text" translate="1" label="Form: text field">
			<key name="label" label="Field label" />
			<key name="placeholder" label="Field placeholder" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/email" translate="1" label="Form: email field">
			<key name="label" label="Field label" />
			<key name="placeholder" label="Field placeholder" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/tel" translate="1" label="Form: phone field">
			<key name="label" label="Field label" />
			<key name="placeholder" label="Field placeholder" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/textarea" translate="1" label="Form: long text field">
			<key name="label" label="Field label" />
			<key name="placeholder" label="Field placeholder" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/select" translate="1" label="Form: dropdown">
			<key name="label" label="Field label" />
			<key name="placeholder" label="First option (placeholder)" />
			<key name="options" label="Options, one per line (keep the order)" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/checkbox" translate="1" label="Form: checkbox">
			<key name="label" label="Checkbox text" />
			<key name="privacyUrl" label="Privacy policy URL" type="link" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/submit" translate="1" label="Form: send button">
			<key name="text" label="Button text" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/notification" translate="1" label="Form: email notification">
			<key name="subject" label="Email subject" />
			<key name="body" label="Email body" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web/whatsapp" translate="1" label="WhatsApp button">
			<key name="message" label="Pre-filled message" />
			<key name="label" label="Button label (screen readers)" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web/map" translate="1" label="Map">
			<key name="placeName" label="Place name" />
			<key name="address" label="Address" />
			<key name="hours" label="Opening hours" />
			<key name="imageAlt" label="Image alternative text" />
			<key name="embedUrl" label="Google Maps embed URL" type="link" />
			<key name="mapsUrl" label="Google Maps link" type="link" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web/carousel" translate="1" label="Carousel">
			<key name="label" label="Carousel name (screen readers)" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-site/consent" translate="1" label="Cookie settings link">
			<key name="label" label="Link text" />
		</gutenberg-block>
	</gutenberg-blocks>
	<!--
		The types of a corporate site (clients, testimonials, locations,
		projects, portfolio) and their metas are NOT declared here since
		17-10-2026: they are definitions of the content-types module (its
		templates), which gives WPML their config through the wpml_config_array
		filter from each definition — the type and taxonomy «wpml» (all
		display-as-translated in the templates) and each field's copy /
		translate (modules/content-types/includes/class-wpml.php). A site that
		changes a mode does it in its definition, in the panel.
		The criterion for the templates' modes is in their files
		(modules/content-types/templates/) and in tests/constructor-pure.test.mjs.
		The trap that stays: WPML's XSD only admits translate="0" or "1" in
		this file (a "2" drops the WHOLE file, admin texts included, with no
		error); modules/site/tests/wpml-config.test.mjs checks the attributes.
	-->
	<!--
		Social module (unpublished): name and link of each network, by
		POSITION in the list («*» is the index). Reordering the list shifts the
		translations; see modules/social/includes/class-links.php. icon and
		icon_id are not translated: they are the same drawing in every
		language.

		Site module (1.4.3): the company details in «Company details»
		(estrategia_web_site) that are written in a language. WPML String
		Translation offers them in WPML › String Translation, domain
		«admin_texts_estrategia_web_site»; untranslated, every language shows
		the original. They reach the site translated through
		Company::value(), so the shortcode, the Block Bindings source and the
		WhatsApp button get them with no code of their own.

		The criterion: a detail goes in if a visitor reads it as a sentence in
		a language (an address says «Nave 14» / «Unit 14», a schedule says
		«Lunes a viernes», the WhatsApp message is a greeting, the registry is
		«Registro Mercantil de…»). Names, numbers, addresses of the internet
		and identifiers do not: Settings::WPML_SAME lists them.

		Edge case, by name: company_name. Even when it is made of words
		(«Lavandería Mallorca») it is a brand and is the same in every
		language; a site whose name really changes per language translates
		the site title (blogname), which WPML already offers.

		The trap: WPML only translates the option on the FRONT (and AJAX), not
		in wp-admin, so the «Company details» screen always shows and saves
		the original; but a REST request (/wp/v2/settings) is not wp-admin,
		and with ?lang=en it reads the translation. Content loads write
		without ?lang (measured 16-10-2026 on Lavandería local, WPML 5.0.2 +
		String Translation 5.0.2). Also: WPML registers the strings when it
		re-reads the files (see above), and only of an option that EXISTS
		then; estrategia_web_site is saved with all its keys, so the empty
		ones (a schedule not filled in yet) are registered too. On a NEW WPML
		install, String Translation builds no translation files (.mo) until
		someone opens WPML › String Translation once: until then a saved
		translation is in the database and the site does not show it
		(measured on a fresh Lavandería local, 16-10-2026). And on
		Playground (SQLite) String Translation builds no .mo and translates
		nothing until its collation cache is cleared: see Lavandería's
		tests/fixtures/lm-test.php. It does not happen on MySQL.

		How to maintain: a new detail in Settings::DEFAULTS goes into
		Settings::WPML_TRANSLATE (and here) or Settings::WPML_SAME, in the same
		commit; modules/site/tests/wpml-config.test.mjs fails otherwise.
	-->
	<admin-texts>
		<key name="estrategia_web_site">
			<key name="registry" />
			<key name="whatsapp_message" />
			<key name="address" />
			<key name="schedule" />
		</key>
		<!--
			WhatsApp module (1.4.3): the button's own message option, used
			when the block's «message» is neither filled in nor bound (the
			parent theme's footer). The phone (estrategia_web_whatsapp_phone)
			is not translated. Lavandería binds the message to the company's
			whatsapp_message above instead.
		-->
		<key name="estrategia_web_whatsapp_message" />
		<key name="estrategia_web_social_links">
			<key name="*">
				<key name="name" />
				<key name="url" />
			</key>
		</key>
	</admin-texts>
</wpml-config>
